# CAD-2026-001 — Business Data Provenance Standard

**Status:** CONSTITUTIONAL · ACCEPTED (2026-07-25)  
**ADR:** `docs/adr/ADR-017-business-data-provenance-cad-2026-001.md`  
**OW register:** `docs/co-arch-003/CO-ARCH-OPPORTUNITY-FIELD-PROVENANCE.md`

## Principle

Every business value displayed in Catalyst One has **exactly one** authoritative source.

Never invent, assume, fabricate, or silently default business information in UI, projections, or adapters.

Uncaptured → **Not Specified** / **Not Selected** / **Pending Input** / editable control.

## Lead & Opportunity stages

**Opportunity Registry** is the only business SSOT.

Must **not** inject business values:

- LoanFile compatibility / caches / stamps
- Runtime projections (structure translation only)
- UI defaults / legacy adapters / placeholder runtime values

## Provenance categories (one per field)

1. Persisted Opportunity Data  
2. User Entered Data  
3. Policy Engine Output  
4. Calculated Business Value  
5. System Metadata  

## Prohibited (unless from an approved source above)

`transactionType = "fresh"` · `lendingType = "secured"` · `requiredAmount = 5000000` · inventing product labels · inventing customer names as business facts

Create-time product defaults are allowed only when **persisted** to Opportunity Registry (explicit create policy), never as silent display invention.

## Deal boundary

Deal / `ensure-loan-workspace` defaults are **Deal runtime** only. They must not feed Opportunity Workspace business display.

## Engineering

Before shipping Opportunity Workspace (or Lead/Opportunity stage) UI: document field provenance or refuse the field.
Do not mark FS-01 FOUNDATION CERTIFIED / FROZEN without Product Owner **"FS-01 Approved"**.
